 produced any long-term  studies I think the longest one has been  a year and we know that that's not a  long-term study maybe in weight weight  loss research that's considered long but  it's really not and so we know that  people have that weight regain within  two to five years  vast majority of people do so you know  it's troubling for me to see their  claims that they are going to help you  lose weight and keep it off for good you  know that's kind of like their tagline  and they have no proof of that you know  I think probably one problem is nobody  wants to be using an app I would assume  for years on end so it's hard for them  to continue tracking everyone Wow  absolutely  yeah it doesn't seem feasible so yeah  very interesting well thank you so much  Caroline for sharing your insights and  kind of behind the scenes in the new  world that's it's really been so  fascinating for us  I'm definitely to be leaving some links  to her website and to Instagram so that  you can reach out for some one-on-one  support so what is my overall take home  on noon well do not be mistaken folks  noon is still a diet and if you've tried  different restrictive weight loss diets  in the past without achieving the  results that you were looking for this  will likely not be any different if you  are truly seeking a positive behavior  change for a healthier lifestyle there  are much better ways to go about it  for example eating plenty of fruits and  vegetables in your day choosing quality  protein sources and choosing whole grain  starches more often than refined also if  you feel that locking your meals is an  effective tool for you and you don't see  any real benefit to those daily readings  or quizzes there are lots of other free  apps that could do the trick and if you  feel drawn to the promise of a greater  attention to the psychological aspects  of eating and behavior change that the  new app always promises I would really  encourage you to reach out to a health  professional like a registered dietician  who can work with you one-on-one to  understand your unique emotional  triggers and strategies all in all if  following the highlighted food rules  calorie budgets and speaking virtually  to a potentially not so well qualified  health coach doesn't seem like the right  path for you I would not recommend zoom  but on that note I would love to hear  your thoughts has noone worked for you  or did you find the app problematic are  there other diets or apps that you want  me to review definitely leave me a  comment below if you like this diet  style review don't forget to give me the  thumbs up and subscribe to the channel  and I'll see you next time on Abby's  kitchen bye  [Music]
 

